# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 7 and the coordinator's ruling FV (`@Flatten` adopts, after the tick its outer fires, the inner the outer then holds, and reads it from the next tick, owed), as sem-ch07-flatten-held's: the inc moves `$a` in its tick; the swap gives the hold the other tuple at 2, whose name the label shows at once; the flatten adopts `$b` after 2 and reads 101 at 3. Never run.
test the_held_tuple_holds_the_dynamic

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="inc")
    1: Ui.Button(label="swap")
    2: Ui.Label(text="0 s")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="1 s")

tick 2
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="1 t")

tick 3
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="101 t")
